2025-05-01 03:46:55 - Thread-1627 (execute) - INFO - [Exploration]
Relevant columns & their potential usage  
• Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021."MetricID": filter on the “Total population” metric (B01003_001E)  
• Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021."CensusValue": the population of an individual block‑group for the chosen metric  
• Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021."BlockGroupID": joins to geography table so the block group can be tied to its tract & state  
• Dim_CensusMetrics."MetricID", "MetricTableDesc": lookup table to verify B01003_001E really is “Total Population”  
• Dim_CensusGeography."BlockGroupID": join to Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021  
• Dim_CensusGeography."StateCountyTractID": the parent tract for each block group – used to roll block‑group values into tract totals  
• Dim_CensusGeography."StateAbbrev" / "StateFIPS": state filter (NY or 36)  
• (optional) Dim_CensusGeography."BlockGroupCode", "TractCode": debugging / exploration columns

Typical conditions that will be useful  
• WHERE "MetricID" = 'B01003_001E'                      -- isolate total population values  
• WHERE "StateAbbrev" = 'NY'                            -- New York only (or "StateFIPS" = '36')  
• GROUP BY "StateCountyTractID"                         -- aggregate to tract level  
• JOIN … ON a."BlockGroupID" = b."BlockGroupID"         -- connect fact & geo tables  

Below are ten incremental Snowflake SQL queries (LIMIT 20 each) that walk from simple exploration to a finished result, all columns are quoted and the fully–qualified table names are used.

```sql
-- 1) Description: Inspect the “Total population” metric definition to make sure we have the right MetricID.
SELECT 
      "MetricID",
      "MetricTableDesc",
      "UnitMeasureType"
FROM   CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusMetrics"
WHERE  "MetricID" = 'B01003_001E'
LIMIT  20;
```

```sql
-- 2) Description: List distinct state abbreviations present in the geography table (sanity‑check that NY exists).
SELECT DISTINCT 
      "StateAbbrev"
FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 3) Description: Peek at raw block‑group population counts regardless of state.
SELECT 
      "BlockGroupID",
      "MetricID",
      "CensusValue"
FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"
WHERE "MetricID" = 'B01003_001E'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 4) Description: Join fact to geography to bring in tract & state; show a few rows.
SELECT 
      f."BlockGroupID",
      g."StateCountyTractID",
      g."StateAbbrev",
      f."CensusValue"
FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f
JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g
      ON f."BlockGroupID" = g."BlockGroupID"
WHERE f."MetricID" = 'B01003_001E'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 5) Description: Same join but restricted to New York State only.
SELECT 
      f."BlockGroupID",
      g."StateCountyTractID",
      g."StateAbbrev",
      f."CensusValue"
FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f
JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g
      ON f."BlockGroupID" = g."BlockGroupID"
WHERE f."MetricID"     = 'B01003_001E'
  AND g."StateAbbrev"  = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 6) Description: Aggregate to get EACH tract’s total population in New York.
SELECT 
      g."StateCountyTractID",
      SUM(f."CensusValue") AS "TotalTractPopulation"
FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f
JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g
      ON f."BlockGroupID" = g."BlockGroupID"
WHERE f."MetricID"    = 'B01003_001E'
  AND g."StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
GROUP BY g."StateCountyTractID"
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 7) Description: Produce both block‑group population and its parent tract total by sub‑selecting the tract aggregates.
SELECT 
      f."BlockGroupID",
      g."StateCountyTractID",
      f."CensusValue"         AS "BlockGroupPop",
      t."TotalTractPopulation"
FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f
JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g
      ON f."BlockGroupID" = g."BlockGroupID"
JOIN (
        SELECT 
              g2."StateCountyTractID",
              SUM(f2."CensusValue") AS "TotalTractPopulation"
        FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f2
        JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g2
              ON f2."BlockGroupID" = g2."BlockGroupID"
        WHERE f2."MetricID"    = 'B01003_001E'
          AND g2."StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
        GROUP BY g2."StateCountyTractID"
     ) AS t
     ON t."StateCountyTractID" = g."StateCountyTractID"
WHERE f."MetricID"    = 'B01003_001E'
  AND g."StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 8) Description: Extend previous query to calculate the population ratio of the block group within its tract.
SELECT 
      f."BlockGroupID",
      g."StateCountyTractID",
      f."CensusValue"                      AS "BlockGroupPop",
      t."TotalTractPopulation",
      f."CensusValue" / NULLIF(t."TotalTractPopulation",0) AS "PopRatio"
FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f
JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g
      ON f."BlockGroupID" = g."BlockGroupID"
JOIN (
        SELECT 
              g2."StateCountyTractID",
              SUM(f2."CensusValue") AS "TotalTractPopulation"
        FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f2
        JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g2
              ON f2."BlockGroupID" = g2."BlockGroupID"
        WHERE f2."MetricID"    = 'B01003_001E'
          AND g2."StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
        GROUP BY g2."StateCountyTractID"
     ) AS t
     ON t."StateCountyTractID" = g."StateCountyTractID"
WHERE f."MetricID"    = 'B01003_001E'
  AND g."StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 9) Description: Same as #8 but sort by the ratio (largest share first) to spot dominant block groups.
SELECT 
      f."BlockGroupID",
      g."StateCountyTractID",
      f."CensusValue"                      AS "BlockGroupPop",
      t."TotalTractPopulation",
      f."CensusValue" / NULLIF(t."TotalTractPopulation",0) AS "PopRatio"
FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f
JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g
      ON f."BlockGroupID" = g."BlockGroupID"
JOIN (
        SELECT 
              g2."StateCountyTractID",
              SUM(f2."CensusValue") AS "TotalTractPopulation"
        FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f2
        JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g2
              ON f2."BlockGroupID" = g2."BlockGroupID"
        WHERE f2."MetricID"    = 'B01003_001E'
          AND g2."StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
        GROUP BY g2."StateCountyTractID"
     ) AS t
     ON t."StateCountyTractID" = g."StateCountyTractID"
WHERE f."MetricID"    = 'B01003_001E'
  AND g."StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
ORDER BY "PopRatio" DESC
LIMIT 20;
```

```sql
-- 10) Description: Final answer query – produce BlockGroupID, block‑group population, StateCountyTractID, tract total population, and population ratio for ALL NY block groups (sampled 20 rows).
SELECT 
      f."BlockGroupID",
      g."StateCountyTractID",
      f."CensusValue"                                            AS "BlockGroupPopulation",
      t."TotalTractPopulation",
      ROUND(f."CensusValue" / NULLIF(t."TotalTractPopulation",0), 6) AS "BlockGroupToTractPopRatio"
FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f
JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g
      ON f."BlockGroupID" = g."BlockGroupID"
JOIN (
        SELECT 
              g2."StateCountyTractID",
              SUM(f2."CensusValue") AS "TotalTractPopulation"
        FROM  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Fact_CensusValues_ACS2021"  AS f2
        JOIN  CENSUS_GALAXY__ZIP_CODE_TO_BLOCK_GROUP_SAMPLE.PUBLIC."Dim_CensusGeography"        AS g2
              ON f2."BlockGroupID" = g2."BlockGroupID"
        WHERE f2."MetricID"    = 'B01003_001E'
          AND g2."StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
        GROUP BY g2."StateCountyTractID"
     ) AS t
     ON t."StateCountyTractID" = g."StateCountyTractID"
WHERE f."MetricID"    = 'B01003_001E'
  AND g."StateAbbrev" = 'NY'
LIMIT 20;
```

These ten queries move step‑by‑step from basic inspection of the metric through joining, filtering, aggregating, and finally calculating each block group’s share of its parent tract’s 2021 ACS total population for New York State.
